note right of dependency
  CHECK: target_type selects exactly one target FK.
  Source and target belong to the same version (composite FK).
  No depends-on cycle inside a version (checked by the service).
end note

note right of application_definition_version
  Immutable: rows of a saved version (and its workloads, resource
  requirements, definitions, dependencies) are never updated or
  deleted. FKs to versions use ON DELETE RESTRICT.
end note

note bottom of delivery_repository
  One per application. IDP creates the repository on the first
  deployment and generates a key pair for this application only.
  Only secret references are stored; keys and the Git hosting
  credential stay in the Secret Store.
end note

note right of application_component
  Stable component IDs across versions. Tables outside a version
  (configuration, instances, workload_deployment) reference these IDs.
  PLATFORM_REQUIREMENT rows (e.g. k8s-cluster, network) are not versioned:
  platform_requirement_type is set only for them; at most one per
  application + type.
end note

note right of catalog_version
  Immutable: a catalog change inserts a new version with all its
  resource_definition rows; UNIQUE (catalog_version_id, name).
  requires must not form cycles (checked when the platform
  loads the version).
end note

note right of configuration_value
  Subtype value objects are embedded in this row.
  CHECK by value_source permits exactly one payload:
  DIRECT -> direct_value;
  RESOURCE_OUTPUT -> resource_requirement_id + resource_output_name;
  WORKLOAD_OUTPUT -> workload_id + workload_output_name.
  No resolved runtime value is stored.
end note

note right of secret
  CHECK permits exactly one source:
  SECRET_REF -> secret_ref, or
  RESOURCE_OUTPUT -> resource_requirement_id + resource_output_name.
  There is no plaintext secret column.
end note

note bottom of resource_instance
  Resource Output is TRANSIENT; therefore no resource_output table exists.
  Partial UNIQUE (application_id, environment, resource_requirement_id,
  deployment_target) WHERE status NOT IN (DESTROYED, UNLINKED).
  infrastructure_reference is not UNIQUE: EXISTING (shared) instances of
  several owners may point to the same real resource.
  Only output_fingerprint is stored, never output values.
  applied_input_fingerprint: input of the last apply (definition of
  the catalog version, parameters, outputs of required platform
  requirements); a different current input means UPDATE.
  applied_overrides is the effective override baseline from the last apply.
end note

note bottom of workload_instance
  Partial UNIQUE (workload_id, environment, deployment_target)
  WHERE status <> REMOVED.
  Kept with status REMOVED after removal. Workload Output is TRANSIENT;
  only output_fingerprint is stored.
end note

note bottom of deployment_execution_job
  Created in the same transaction as the CAS
  deployment.status AWAITING_CONFIRMATION -> CONFIRMED.
  Job status literals and worker recovery are deferred (D6).
end note

@enduml
